<article class="env-lemma" id="00XX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00XX">Lemma <span data-tag="00XX">7.22.1</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ and $\mathcal{D}$ be sites. Let $u : \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{D}$, and $v : \mathcal{D} \to \mathcal{C}$ be functors. Assume that $u$ is cocontinuous and that $v$ is a right adjoint to $u$. Let $g : \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}) \to \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{D})$ be the morphism of topoi associated to $u$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/00XO" data-tag="00XO">7.21.1</a>. Then </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
for a sheaf $\mathcal{F}$ on $\mathcal{C}$ the sheaf $g_*\mathcal{F}$ is equal to the presheaf $v^ p\mathcal{F}$, in other words, $(g_*\mathcal{F})(V) = \mathcal{F}(v(V))$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for a sheaf $\mathcal{G}$ on $\mathcal{D}$ we have $g^{-1}\mathcal{G} = (v_ p\mathcal{G})^\# $. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      For $\mathcal{F}$ as in (1) we have 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  g_*\mathcal{F} = {}_ su\mathcal{F} = {}_ pu\mathcal{F} = v^ p\mathcal{F} = \mathcal{F} \circ v  \]
</div>
    <p>
       The first equality is Lemma <a href="/tag/00XO" data-tag="00XO">7.21.1</a>. The second equality is Lemma <a href="/tag/00XK" data-tag="00XK">7.20.2</a>. The third equality is Lemma <a href="/tag/09VQ" data-tag="09VQ">7.19.3</a>. The final equality is the definition of $v^ p$ in Section <a href="/tag/00VC" data-tag="00VC">7.5</a>. This proves (1). For $\mathcal{G}$ as in (2) we have 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  g^{-1}\mathcal{G} = (u^ p\mathcal{G})^\#  = (v_ p\mathcal{G})^\#   \]
</div>
    <p>
       The first equality is Lemma <a href="/tag/00XO" data-tag="00XO">7.21.1</a>. The second equality is Lemma <a href="/tag/09VQ" data-tag="09VQ">7.19.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>